{"toolCallId":"exec:1#6c4c3a17ffb14b259a9c6d0d4874b3ed","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS | error | always | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED | error | always | Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER | error | always | Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | error | always | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY | error | always | Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nLEVEL_DECLARED | info | always | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | info | always | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE | error | always | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nANCHORS_VALID | error | always | Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK | error | always | Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY | error | always | Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY | error | always | Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION | error | always | Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT | error | always | Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY | error | always | Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS | error | always | Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | error | always | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING | error | always | Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | error | always | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES | warn | always | Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\nSOURCE_TAGS | warn | always | Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\nGREP_CONVENTION | error | always | Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH | error | always | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT | warn | always | Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT | warn | always | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY | error | always | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | warn | always | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY | error | always | Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | warn | always | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nNORMALIZER_LINT | error | always | Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY | error | always | Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE | error | always | Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | error | always | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | error | always | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | error | always | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED | error | always | Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS | error | always | Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | error | strict-only | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | error | strict-only | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | error | strict-only | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\nLINKS_VALID | warn | always | Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d8a6af","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
